# Keys that save typing
> At the vsh prompt (not at the tutorial prompt) the line editor helps you type:
> Up and Down walk through earlier lines, Ctrl-R searches them as you type, Tab completes
> a command or a file name (Tab again lists the choices), the grey text after the cursor is
> a suggestion from your history (Right or End takes it), Ctrl-L clears the window, and
> Ctrl-C stops a running command. Try them after this lesson, at the vsh prompt.
? Print the word history with echo, then try Up at the vsh prompt later.
= case "$LEARN_LINE" in "echo history") true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ Type echo history.
! echo history
? Print the word complete with echo.
= case "$LEARN_LINE" in "echo complete") true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ Type echo complete.
! echo complete
